  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance for Myanmar Muslims from Rakhine State and Special At-Risk Groups in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian needs and protection risks of Myanmar Muslims from Rakhine State and special at-risk groups have continued to increase in the region, including Thailand, without sufficient legal or protection support available to them. Through this project, the IOM is contributing to the protection of Myanmar Muslims from Rakhine State&#x202f;and special at-risk groups in Thailand through direct humanitarian assistance. The project contributed to the improved physical and psychosocial well-being of migrants through physical health assistance, mental health and psychosocial support, food and supplemental nutrition, non-food items, and water, sanitation and hygiene. Furthermore, the project strengthens coordination with government and non-governmental partners to promote delivery of humanitarian assistance and to address protection concerns among beneficiaries. IOM will coordinate with the Royal Thai Government and humanitarian partners to assess and address the humanitarian and protection needs of project beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
